  {
   "id": "n003",
   "legacy_id": "M1",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "level": "L3",
   "content": {
    "text": "Global finance is shifting back onto bank balance sheets because non-bank finance cannot offer stability in a crisis, straining banks with Fed and ECB access.",
    "label": null,
    "explicit": true,
    "reason": "In crises, funding migrates to institutions with central bank access, straining their balance sheets."
   },
   "source": {
    "passages": [
     {
      "paragraph_id": "p5",
      "relation": "states",
      "link_method": "llm_citation",
      "anchor_grade": "excerpt",
      "review_status": "pending",
      "source_excerpt": "Global finance is now quickly being re-intermediated through banks, as they offer a form of stability that the “shadow” (non-bank) financial system cannot replicate in a crisis."
     }
    ]
   },
   "facets": {
