  {
   "id": "n004",
   "legacy_id": "M2",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "level": "L3",
   "content": {
    "text": "The shocks can offset one another: an oil importer like Turkey gains from cheap energy but loses export, tourism and bank rollover funding.",
    "label": null,
    "explicit": true,
    "reason": "A country's net exposure is the sum of its gains and losses across simultaneous shocks."
   },
   "source": {
    "passages": [
     {
      "paragraph_id": "p6",
      "relation": "states",
      "link_method": "llm_citation",
      "anchor_grade": "excerpt",
      "review_status": "pending",
      "source_excerpt": "These shocks can have offsetting impacts. A country that imports oil, for example, Turkey, will benefit from lower energy prices."
     }
    ]
   },
   "facets": {
