    "text": "Saudi Arabia and Russia each hold about $500 billion in reserves, the smaller GCC states over $1 trillion in sovereign funds, and Taiwan has far more foreign assets than foreign liabilities.",
    "label": null,
    "explicit": true,
    "reason": "The size of reserves relative to likely shortfalls measures capacity to self-finance."
